{%- comment -%}
  One library item's README, rendered by `library-readmes.ts` into the
  `kg:subgraph` marker region of `<library>/<slug>/README.md` — the same
  region, and the same rule, as bootstrap's subgraph READMEs: the platform
  owns the markers, never the file.

  Every value is read from the item's own `manifest.jsonld` or counted on
  disk; nothing is composed:
    item    slug, title, disposition, provenance, docId, sourceFile,
            sha256 (first 12), pages, arxiv, doi
    counts  sections, blocks, images — files present under the item
    library the declared library it sits in: id (its path in the
            repository), readme (relative link)
{%- endcomment -%}
